invariant: INV-17
file: src/chacha20.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: chacha20_block returns without wiping its state, whose words 4 to
  11 are the key, so its dead frame keeps the key side by side. aead.c keys
  Poly1305 through it for every message. Every block it writes is still
  right. bin/chacha20_equiv_test copies the stack below a call and looks
  for the key.

--- old
    block(state, out);
    ct_wipe(state, sizeof state);
--- new
    block(state, out);
